   "record": "c447c304498f50167b7d43b1b58ad5c7b22897f860a8e618bd19cc66a8af21fa",
   "status": "MISMATCH",
   "ruling": "Ruling: ambiguity; amb.2025.f1116_carryover_election and coordinator decision D3 (docs/provisional/DECISIONS.md, X1-F1116: the election made whenever its conditions are met). i1116 pp. 1-2: with the election \"You can't carry over to or from any other year any foreign taxes\". The model reads the election as the filer's choice and notes that electing forfeits any excess of foreign tax over the regular tax that Form 1116 would carry forward. The recorded reading and D3 make the election whenever available; on this tool's Form 1116 path any such excess refuses (f1116.carryover_out, coordinator decision D1), so a No could only refuse the return. The English states what the project does. Raised for the owner in the report: whether to refuse instead of electing when ftc.taxes exceeds ftc.regular_tax, which keeps the carryforward the election forfeits.",
